  "id": "Compound::DB00145 - Gene::2741",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence from the hetionet dataset strongly suggests a mechanistic link between Glycine and Glra1, supported by multiple pathways involving the extracellular-glycine-gated ion channel activity. Glycine binds to Glra3 and Glra2, which are both involved in the regulation of extracellular-glycine-gated ion channels, and these channels are ultimately associated with Glra1. This indicates that Glycine may modulate the activity of Glra1 through a shared pathway involving glycine-gated ion channels. The high scores in all three paths suggest a consistent and robust relationship, with Glycine acting as a ligand that influences the function of Glra1 via a common mechanism of glycine-gated ion channel activation. The presence of multiple independent pathways reinforcing this connection strengthens the hypothesis that Glycine and Glra1 are functionally linked through a shared biological process.",
